Abstract = {Acute premacular bleeding is often associated with vasoproliferative
   retinal changes, vascular anomalies or a Valsalva maneuver. The
   diagnosis is made during the funduscopic examination and can if
   necessary be confirmed with optical coherence tomography (OCT). This
   article presents a case example with a sub-inner limiting membrane
