Month = {NOV},
Abstract = {Pediatric atopic dermatitis (AD) is one of the most common dermatoses
   encountered by health-care providers treating children. Diagnosis of AD
   is clinical, with no universally accepted biomarkers or assessment
   tools. Patient-reported outcomes and subjective assessments of quality
   of life in both the patient and family are important considerations when
   treating pediatric AD. Here, we provide an overview of pediatric AD
   epidemiology, its clinical presentation, burden, diagnosis, and
   assessment, with a focus on implications for patient counseling in order
   to optimize care.},
