Year = {2001},
Volume = {11},
Number = {3},
Pages = {203-216},
Month = {OCT},
Abstract = {Monitoring and evaluation of forestry projects is needed to accurately
   determine their impact on greenhouse gas emissions and other attributes,
   and to ensure that the global climate is protected and that country
   obligations are met. We present an overview of guidelines recently
   developed for the monitoring, evaluation, reporting, verification, and
   certification of forestry projects for climate change mitigation.(1)
   These guidelines are targeted to developers, evaluators, verifiers, and
   certifiers of forestry projects, and address several key issues,
   including methods for estimating gross and net carbon savings. The next
   phase of our work will be to develop a procedural handbook providing
   information on how one can complete monitoring, evaluation and
   verification forms. We then plan to test the usefulness of these
   handbooks in the real world. (C) 2001 Elsevier Science Ltd. All rights
